  "reason": "These values come from hand-built strong-field d5 matrices with C/B = 4.341: 3×3 matrices for 4T1 and 4T2, and a 7×7 matrix for 2T2 that leaves out the weakly coupled t2^2e^3 and t2e^4 states, so the 2T2 values carry an estimated error of about ±0.5B. On this basis 6A1 is the ground term at Dq/B = 1.45 and 2.55, 2T2 becomes the ground term after the crossover at Dq/B ≈ 2.76, and the 2A2, 2T1, 4A1 and 4E terms stay higher at all three points."
